    fix(conformance): publish marker v2 writer golden (#15)
    
    * release: prepare protocol suite v1.0.0-rc.6
    
    * Publish the marker-v2 writer golden
    
    Managers write install marker schema 2 for every schema 1 through 6
    installation mutation, but the shared fixture published only
    expected/marker.json, the frozen marker-v1 legacy-read evidence. A
    downstream consumer comparing its own writer output against that file
    sees a schema mismatch it cannot resolve without either rewriting
    release history or dropping the writer assertion.
    
    Publish expected/marker-v2.json, generated from the same golden
    installation with exactly schema_version, build_roots and builds
    changed. The golden skill activates no compiled command, so builds is
    empty and build_source stays absent. expected/marker.json is untouched.
    
    The validator and the rc.6 release gate now require the writer golden,
    reject an in-place edit of the frozen legacy marker, and reject a writer
    golden that carries build state the fixture has none of, declares
    build_source without builds, leaves the schema 1 through 6 range, or
    describes a different installation.
    
    * Advance the Curator implementation pin
    
    Move the Go manager pin to fee35c87, whose interop gate reads the
    manager-lifecycle vector by case name and therefore accepts the rc.6 dry-run
    case compiled-cache-miss-is-read-only. The previous pin 17804ce required
    exactly two dry-run cases, so Implementations failed on every runner at its
    first step. The new pin is the immutable full commit ID of relux-works/curator
    PR 9 and advances to the merged main commit once that PR lands.
    
    * Pin the Curator PR head
    
    Move the Go manager pin from fee35c87 to the head of relux-works/curator PR 9,
    bd6ba08, so the pin is the commit that lands. It carries the same lifecycle
    gate plus the toolchain-identity repair that unblocks Curator's own CI, and
    changes nothing the Implementations job reads.
